Q: Map&lt;?, Optional&lt;T&gt;&gt; to Map&lt;?, T&gt; A: <p>Here is a generic function which achieves the goal:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>private static &lt;K, T&gt; Map&lt;K, T&gt; convert(Map&lt;K, Optional&lt;T&gt;&gt; input) {
    return input.entrySet().stream()
            .flatMap(e -&gt; e.getValue().stream().map(v -&gt; Map.entry(e.getKey(), v)))
            .collect(Collectors.toMap(Map.Entry::getKey, Map.Entry::getValue));
}
</code></pre>
<p>This converts each <code>Optional</code> to a <code>Stream</code> of zero or one <code>Entry&lt;K, Optional&lt;T&gt;&gt;</code> using <code>Optional.stream</code>.  These mapped entries — none of which are empty — are each mapped to an <code>Entry&lt;K, T&gt;</code> containing the unwrapped <code>Optional</code>.  Finally, the <code>Entry</code> elements are converted back to a <code>Map</code> using <code>Collectors.toMap</code>.</p>

Q: jquery var equals var doesnt work A: <p>It's very likely that <code>recentposttitle</code> has extra whitespace. If you have HTML like</p>
<pre><code>    &lt;h2 class=&quot;post-title&quot;&gt;
    This is the title
    &lt;/h2&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>there will be newline and space characters at the beginning and end. You should remove these before comparing:</p>
<pre><code>var recentposttitle = $('#catblogoutput h2.post-title').text().trim();
</code></pre>
